# What must not enter the image.
#
# The first two lines are the ones that matter: a checkout holds a live database and its caches,
# and `COPY . /app` would bake somebody's library metadata into an image that is meant to be
# reproducible. Everything else here is state, tests or tooling that the server never reads.
.git
.gitignore
hardlylistening.db
hardlylistening.db-wal
hardlylistening.db-shm
.cache
artist-art
backups
tmp
deploy
tests
docs
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.log